1. DEFINITIONS

   "Software"   this codebase, including the admin panel, storefront,
                database schema and accompanying files.
   "Licensor"   New Aeon.
   "Licensee"   the individual or organisation named on the invoice or
                order form under which this Software was supplied.
   "Instance"   one running deployment of the Software serving one website.
   "Licence"    this agreement.


2. GRANT

   Subject to payment of the applicable fee, the Licensor grants the Licensee
   a non-exclusive, non-transferable, worldwide licence to:

   (a) install and run the Software as ONE Instance in production, together
       with any number of non-production copies used solely for development,
       staging, testing or backup;

   (b) modify the Software for the Licensee's own use, including changing
       appearance, adding features, and integrating other systems; and

   (c) receive the source code, which is required in order to exercise (a)
       and (b).

   Each additional production Instance requires an additional licence.


3. RESTRICTIONS

   The Licensee shall not:

   (a) sell, sublicense, lease, rent, lend or otherwise distribute the
       Software, or any derivative of it, to any third party;

   (b) operate the Software as a multi-tenant service, hosting platform or
       website builder from which third parties obtain their own sites,
       except under a separate written agreement with the Licensor;

   (c) publish the source code, in whole or in substantial part, in any
       public repository or other public location; or

   (d) remove or obscure copyright notices in the source code.

   Clause 3(d) concerns notices in the CODE. Visible branding in the admin
   panel and on the storefront is addressed in clause 4.


4. BRANDING

   Unless the Licensee holds a white-label licence, the Software may display
   an attribution to the Licensor within the admin panel. That attribution
   is not shown to visitors of the public website, and the Licensee is free
   to present the public site entirely under their own brand.

   A white-label licence removes the admin attribution and permits the
   Licensee to present the Software as their own product to their clients.


5. AGENCY AND CLIENT WORK

   An agency licensee may install and configure an Instance on behalf of a
   client, and may charge that client for the work. The licence for that
   Instance must be held by either the agency or the client, and one licence
   covers one Instance regardless of which of them holds it.

   Delivering the source code to the client for whom the Instance was built
   is permitted, and does not constitute distribution under clause 3(a).
   That client is then bound by this Licence in respect of that Instance.


